criteria:
The self-hosted option is described on all four dimensions using the same units that will be used for the managed options:
- monthly cost (USD/month at current volume);
- p95 query latency (ms);
- operational effort (hours/month or an equivalent stated measure);
- migration effort, marked not applicable.

Each managed option has an entry for all four dimensions:
- monthly cost at the WI-1 baseline volume;
- p95 query latency, with the measurement method stated;
- operational effort;
- rough migration effort.

The units match the self-hosted baseline.

work_items.description:
Scope: Synthesize the WI-1 and WI-2 results into a short written recommendation for the architecture review on 20 October.

Expected behavior: The document contains:
- a comparison table covering self-hosted plus the 2–3 managed options across the four dimensions;
- the trade-offs between the options;
- a recommendation;
- the unresolved questions and data gaps (Q2–Q6) and assumptions.

The recommendation is advisory only and does not commit to a migration.

Bounded approach: The whole investigation, from start to finished document, must not exceed two weeks. Q6 (the review year and template) is unresolved and non-blocking. A short document is produced, and the missing template or format is noted rather than assumed.

criteria:
A short written recommendation document exists. It contains:
